- The North African Campaign, which began in June 1940 and involved British air and sea forces based on Malta attacking Axis ships transporting vital supplies and reinforcements from Europe.
- The Battle of the Mediterranean, which involved continuous Allied attacks on German forces in northern Italy and occupied Yugoslavia, ultimately leading to their retreat by April 1945.
- The Balkans Campaign, where the National Liberation Army of Yugoslavia, assisted by Western Allies, battled Axis powers on the opposite side of the Adriatic Sea, eventually joining forces with the advancing Soviet Army to push remaining German forces out of the Balkans.
