-   The tricuspid valve's leaflets are connected to the papillary muscles via chordae tendineae, which help to prevent the leaflets from prolapsing into the right atrium during ventricular systole (contraction phase).
-   During ventricular systole, the tricuspid valve closes, preventing backflow of blood from the right ventricle into the right atrium.

