Identify the creator of the One Ring in J.R.R. Tolkien's Lord of the Rings series, including their motivations and background.
The creator of the One Ring in J.R.R. Tolkien's Lord of the Rings series is Sauron, the Dark Lord. 

Sauron's motivations for creating the One Ring were to gain dominion over Middle-earth. He intended to use the Ring to control the other Rings of Power, which he had created or influenced the Elves to create, and thereby subvert the free will of the peoples of Middle-earth to his power. 

Sauron's background is that of a powerful and malevolent being who sought to conquer and enslave all of Middle-earth. He was a Maia, one of the powerful beings created by the Valar (angelic beings) in J.R.R. Tolkien's mythology, but he was corrupted by the Dark Lord Morgoth and became a servant of darkness.
