Identify the correct organization and leadership structure of the International Cricket Council (ICC).
The International Cricket Council (ICC) is a global governing body of cricket with the following organization and leadership structure:

- The ICC has 105 members, consisting of 12 Full Members and 93 Associate Members.
- The ICC is headed by a Chairman who leads the board of directors.
- The Chairman is responsible for overseeing the organization and governance of cricket's major international tournaments, including the Cricket World Cup.
- The ICC also has an Anti-Corruption and Security Unit (ACSU) that coordinates action against corruption and match-fixing in international cricket.

Note that the ICC does not control bilateral fixtures between member countries, domestic cricket in member countries, or the laws of the game, which remain under the control of the Marylebone Cricket Club.
