What are the legal frameworks and authorities that govern the issuance of search warrants in various jurisdictions?
The legal frameworks and authorities that govern the issuance of search warrants in various jurisdictions include:

1.  In most countries, a search warrant is issued by a magistrate or judge, as stated in the context of "Search warrant".
2.  In the United States, search warrants are determined under Title 18 of the United States Code and extended under Rule 41 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure.
3.  Each state in the United States has its own laws and rules of procedure governing the issuance of warrants, as mentioned in the context of "Search warrant".
4.  In Russia, the authority to issue search and arrest warrants was transferred from the Procuracy to the courts as part of the new Code, as stated in the context of "Politics of Russia".

These legal frameworks and authorities are in place to ensure that search warrants are issued in accordance with the law and respect the right to privacy.
