The DREAM Act is an American legislative proposal for a multi-phase process for qualifying alien minors in the United States. It was first introduced in the Senate on August 1, 2001, by United States Senators Dick Durbin (D- Illinois) and Orrin Hatch (R- Utah). The bill proposes to grant conditional residency to qualifying alien minors, with the possibility of permanent residency upon meeting further qualifications. Despite being reintroduced several times, the DREAM Act has failed to pass.
