Investigate the legislative history of the EAHCA, including its passage and amendments, to understand its development and evolution.
The Education for All Handicapped Children Act (EAHCA) was enacted by the United States Congress in 1975. It was initially passed as Public Law (PL) 94-142. 

The act received amendments in 1986 and 1992, which encouraged states to develop programs for individuals with disabilities and guaranteed educational rights from any institution receiving federal funding.

In 1997, the EAHCA was revised and became the Individuals with Disabilities Education Act (IDEA).
