What are the distinctive sonic elements of the G-Funk sound, and how did they differ from other hip-hop sub-genres of the time?
The distinctive sonic elements of the G-Funk sound include:

1. Multi-layered and melodic synthesizers
2. Slow hypnotic grooves
3. Deep bass
4. Background female vocals
5. Extensive sampling of P-Funk tunes
6. High-pitched portamento saw wave synthesizer lead

These elements, particularly the use of funk with an artificially altered tempo and the incorporation of live musicians to replay sampled records, set G-Funk apart from other hip-hop sub-genres of the time, such as the Bay Area-based sound known as Mobb music.
