What were the last recorded instances of the guillotine's use in France, including the date, location, and any notable events or figures involved?
The last recorded instances of the guillotine's use in France were:

1. Christian Ranucci, a child-murderer, who was executed on 28 July 1976 in Marseille.
2. Jérôme Carrein, who was executed on 23 June 1977 in Douai.
3. Hamida Djandoubi, a torturer-murderer, who was executed on 10 September 1977.

Additionally, the last public guillotining in France was of Eugen Weidmann, who was convicted of six murders and was beheaded on 17 June 1939 outside the prison Saint-Pierre, rue Georges Clemenceau 5 at Versailles.
