What is the historical context of the Beauty and the Beast story, including its literary and cultural influences, and the time period in which it was first written or published?
The Beauty and the Beast story has its historical context rooted in the 18th century. It was first written by French novelist Gabrielle-Suzanne Barbot de Villeneuve and published in 1740 in "La Jeune Américaine et les contes marins" (The Young American and Marine Tales). 

The story was later abridged and rewritten by Jeanne-Marie Leprince de Beaumont in 1756 in "Magasin des enfants" (Children's Collection). This version is the one most commonly retold. 

The story was influenced by earlier tales, such as "Cupid and Psyche" and "The Golden Ass". It has been said that Gabrielle was inspired by the tale "Cupid and Psyche". 

The story gained international acclaim over the years and was later adapted into a Disney movie in 1991.
